{"_id":"6a2ff7132204ffbc59e5a6ef","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"ucEFYVtXIvuYKjudK3pwB","description":"# IQR\n\nThe Interquartile Range (IQR) is the difference between the 75th percentile (Q3) and 25th percentile (Q1) of a dataset. Outliers are commonly defined as values below Q1 ΓêÆ 1.5├ùIQR or above Q3 + 1.5├ùIQR. The IQR method is robust to extreme values and is the basis for the box plot's whiskers.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Using Pandas IQR: 3 Essential Steps","url":"https://medium.com/@heyamit10/using-pandas-iqr-3-essential-steps-f5cf73a390ba","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaf1"},{"type":"article","title":"How to detect outliers using IQR and Boxplots?","url":"https://machinelearningplus.com/machine-learning/how-to-detect-outliers-using-iqr-and-boxplots/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaf2"},{"type":"video","title":"Outlier detection and removal using IQR","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A3gClkblXK8","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaf3"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:58:59.081Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/ucEFYVtXIvuYKjudK3pwB.md"}